Richard,

Leslie, Miguel, Keith and I checked 28 proposed facts this afternoon. Twenty-=
five are supported within the limits in the source table; three remain on hol=
d for the copy.

For Alder FY23 CO-02, the execution signatures do not establish the delegated=
 decision date. Leslie is pursuing the dated decision. For Mill, the 840 squa=
re yards in the schedule and Keller's material is a planned quantity, not a c=
ompleted measurement; Miguel is looking for the measurement book. For Quarry =
CO-01, the September 28 traffic preparation sheet has a blank construction-wo=
rk field, so it cannot tell us whether the changed work started before the Oc=
tober 3 signatures. Keith is seeking a contemporaneous signed or confirmed wo=
rk record.

The attached PDF is the short hold memo for the desk read. The separate workb=
ook traces all 28 claims to their pages or times and records their limits. Pl=
ease keep these three assertions out of the copy while we follow up; I will r=
echeck any new records.

Veronica

